  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates which lottery has a higher probability of its minimum outcome and prefers that lottery. In this case, Lottery A has a 100% probability of its minimum (and only) outcome (2400 Euros), while Lottery B has a 1% probability of its minimum outcome (0 Euros). The reason would thus prefer Lottery A. However, the individual chooses Lottery B *because* the probability of the minimum outcome (0 Euros) is low, interpreting this as a positive feature. This is the inverse of the decision reason: the individual prefers the lottery with the *lower* probability of the minimum outcome, not the higher. Therefore, while the individual considers the same piece of information (probability of the minimum outcome), they apply the opposite logic to it. The decision reason is not used; instead, a different reasoning rule is applied—avoiding low-probability losses rather than favoring high-probability minimums.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

